# Concord Voice Docker Compose Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and adjust values for your environment.
# concord-dev.sh up will auto-copy this file to .env if .env does not exist.
#
# PRODUCTION: Do NOT use these values. Use provision-secrets.yml to set
# real secrets via GitHub environment secrets.

# PostgreSQL
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=concord_dev_password

# Redis
REDIS_PASSWORD=concord_dev_redis

# JWT Secret (MUST change in production)
JWT_SECRET=dev_jwt_secret_change_in_production

# TURN/STUN (coturn)
TURN_SECRET=concord_dev_turn_secret
# PUBLIC_IP is REQUIRED. coturn advertises this address in CANDIDATE/ALLOCATION
# responses — clients connect back to it for relayed media. For local dev set
# it to your LAN IP (e.g. 192.168.1.42); for production set it to the host's
# public IPv4. In production this is written automatically by provision-secrets.yml
# from the `server_host` workflow input. If unset, docker compose will refuse to start.
PUBLIC_IP=127.0.0.1

# Object Storage (MinIO)
MINIO_ROOT_USER=concord
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=concord_dev_minio

# pgAdmin (optional, dev tools profile)
PGADMIN_PASSWORD=admin

# Strict-Transport-Security policy emitted by the control-plane for Go-proxied
# production responses (#2318/#2374). Optional; empty uses the strong default.
# In direct/self-host paths this changes Go-proxied responses; the committed
# nginx render keeps its default on nginx-generated/scoped responses. Managed
# hosts instead render the same value once at the public nginx edge.
HSTS_HEADER_VALUE=

# Activity History (#1235) — fail closed until a drained operator activation.
# CONTROL_PLANE_REPLICA_COUNT is enforced unconditionally since #2178: any
# explicitly set value other than 1 fails control-plane startup regardless of the
# gate below. The WebSocket hub holds session state and channel interest maps in
# process memory, so a second replica silently drops cross-replica fanout.
# Horizontal scaling is tracked in #2757.
ACTIVITY_HISTORY_CLUSTER_ENABLED=false
CONTROL_PLANE_REPLICA_COUNT=1
# Self-hosted operators must provide their own disclosure. Empty keeps consent
# unavailable; never substitute Concord Voice LLC for another operator.
ACTIVITY_HISTORY_OPERATOR_NAME=
ACTIVITY_HISTORY_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL=

# NUM_WORKERS (mediasoup worker count) is deliberately NOT an env-file variable
# (#2178). It is a compose literal in each file's media-plane environment: block
# — "4" in docker-compose.yml, "3" in docker-compose.production.yml, sized to
# that file's cpus limit — so it never enters an env file and carries none of the
# five env-var surfaces. It is validated fail-closed at media-plane startup: a
# value that is not an integer >= 1 logs FATAL and exits 1.

# --- GIF integration (KLIPY) ---
# Documentation only — these are NOT new variables. The control-plane has read
# both since #2371 and the KLIPY block of [internal]deploy.env.example has
# always carried them; this file simply never did, so a local dev stack came up
# with no GIFs and no indication why (#2369).
#
# KLIPY_API_KEY enables the whole integration. With it empty the control-plane
# registers NO /klipy routes at all and the desktop client's gifsEnabled flag
# mirrors that, so the picker and every GIF embed are absent rather than broken.
# Anything that has to be verified against real GIF traffic — including this
# feature's own pause/resume network checks — is unrunnable until it is set.
#
# KLIPY_CUSTOMER_ID_KEY (#2371) keys the HMAC that derives KLIPY's per-user
# partition key from the authenticated user id, so the value a client sends is
# a rotation nonce rather than an identity and cannot address another user's
# recent-GIF ledger. OPTIONAL: when empty the derivation falls back to
# KLIPY_API_KEY, which is safe — the routes do not exist without that key — but
# the two are then coupled, and ROTATING KLIPY_API_KEY CHANGES EVERY DERIVED ID
# AND EMPTIES EVERY USER'S RECENT TAB. Set it to decouple them. Any
# high-entropy value works: openssl rand -hex 32
# KLIPY_API_KEY=
# KLIPY_CUSTOMER_ID_KEY=

# --- Stripe billing (#2033) ---
# Documentation only: leave every line commented for an ordinary dev stack.
# BILLING_PURCHASE_MODE defaults to off and both keys to empty, so no billing
# path runs. For a local test-mode soak, set a TEST key (rk_test_... preferred,
# or sk_test_...) and the whsec_... signing secret of the endpoint that
# delivers to this stack. A live key fails startup unless ENVIRONMENT=production,
# and a test key fails it when ENVIRONMENT=production. Every rule is in
# services/control-plane/pkg/config/billing.go and is mirrored by
# [internal]check-billing-env.sh; both run the cases in
# services/control-plane/pkg/config/testdata/billing_env_cases.tsv.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# BILLING_PURCHASE_MODE=off
# BILLING_PURCHASE_ALLOWLIST=
# FOUNDERS_PRICING_ENDS_AT=
# STRIPE_AUTOMATIC_TAX=false
